# Non-secret local codesigning contract for scripts/package.sh.
#
# macOS TCC (Accessibility, Screen Recording) remembers a grant by the app's
# designated requirement, not by its path. An ad-hoc signature has no stable
# certificate, so every rebuild produces a new code identity and macOS treats
# the result as a brand-new app that has to be approved again. Signing with a
# persistent certificate keeps the designated requirement identical across
# rebuilds, so a granted permission survives reinstalls.
#
# DESKBAR_SIGN_IDENTITY is the SHA-1 fingerprint reported by
#   security find-identity -v -p codesigning
# not a keychain display name. This is the same local self-signed certificate
# the adjacent session-manager repo signs sm-server with
# (config/rust-server-signing.env there).
#
# DESKBAR_SIGN_DESIGNATED_REQUIREMENT is the exact requirement the signature is
# expected to carry, captured from `codesign -d -r-` on a signed bundle. It is
# checked after signing so a certificate swap can never silently change the
# identity TCC keyed the existing grants to.
#
# On a machine without this certificate, package.sh warns and falls back to
# ad-hoc signing so a fresh clone still builds. Set DESKBAR_REQUIRE_SIGNING=1 to
# turn that fallback into a hard failure.
DESKBAR_SIGN_IDENTITY=36FC54A873D584A34FCFEEA7D1F519B19A39DE72
DESKBAR_SIGN_IDENTIFIER=com.deskbar.app
DESKBAR_SIGN_DESIGNATED_REQUIREMENT=designated => identifier "com.deskbar.app" and certificate root = H"36fc54a873d584a34fcfeea7d1f519b19a39de72"
